  "usage_note": "**Rightly** is a different word: it means *for a good reason* (*She was rightly angry*), not *correctly*. After a verb of movement, the adverb **right** takes no **the**: *turn right*, but *turn to the right*.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "Turn to right at the end of the street.",
      "correct": "Turn right at the end of the street.",
      "note": "Use **turn right**, or **turn to the right** with **the**; not **to right**."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "She right answered the question.",
      "correct": "She answered the question right.",
      "note": "In the sense *correctly*, **right** comes after the verb, and after its object if it has one, never before the verb."
    }
